{"ISBN:9789004270121":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9789004270121","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL28354072M/Dionysos_in_Classical_Athens","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL28354072M/Dionysos_in_Classical_Athens","details":{"publishers":["Brill"],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"\"Dionysos, with his following of satyrs and women, was a major theme in a big part of the figure painted pottery in 500-300 B.C. Athens. As an original testimonial of their time, the imagery on these vases convey what this god meant to his worshippers. It becomes clear that he was not only appropriate for wine, wine indulgence, ecstasy and theatre. Rather, he was presenton many, both happy and sad, occasions. The vase painters have emphasized different aspects of Dionysos for their customers inside and outside of Athens, depending on the political and cultural situation.\""},"source_records":["marc:marc_oapen/oapen.marc.utf8.mrc:2226543:1380","marc:marc_oapen/convert_oapen_20201117.mrc:19391426:1677","bwb:9789004270121"],"title":"Dionysos in Classical Athens","notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Knowledge Unlatched 102231 KU Select 2018: HSS Backlist Books\n\nEnglish."},"links":[{"url":"http://www.oapen.org/download?type=document&docid=1005258","title":"Access full text online"},{"url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/legalcode","title":"Creative Commons License"}],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"subjects":["History of religion"],"publish_country":"xx","key":"/books/OL28354072M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL5949448A","name":"Cornelia Isler-Kerényi"}],"isbn_13":["9789004270121"],"works":[{"key":"/works/OL20927476W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"lc_classifications":["BL820.B2 I7 2014"],"latest_revision":3,"revision":3,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2020-07-21T03:24:57.925367"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2021-09-29T18:07:28.383513"}}},"ISBN:9788490962466":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9788490962466","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL28354145M/Missions_d'évangélisation_et_circulation_des_savoirs","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL28354145M/Missions_d'évangélisation_et_circulation_des_savoirs","details":{"publishers":["Casa de Velázquez"],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Quels furent les savoirs utilisés, diffusés et produits par les missionnaires catholiques, à partir du milieu du XVIe siècle, aussi bien en Europe, qu'en Amérique, en Asie et en Afrique ? Dans quelle mesure l'entreprise d'évangélisation des âmes, jugées par les missionnaires comme païennes, hérétiques ou simplement indifférentes, a-t-elle participé à l'aventure moderne de la circulation des savoirs ? Ces questions intéressent aussi bien l'histoire sociale et culturelle des missions que l'histoire des empires et des sociétés coloniales ou l'histoire intellectuelle. Elles conduisent à réfléchir sur la manière dont l'Europe, à l'époque moderne, est entrée en relation avec d'autres espaces. À la croisée des croyances et des connaissances, les missions d'évangélisation ont suscité de profonds changements dans l'architecture des savoirs et ont paradoxalement participé à la sécularisation de la conception du monde."},"source_records":["marc:marc_oapen/oapen.marc.utf8.mrc:2334283:1982","marc:marc_oapen/convert_oapen_20201117.mrc:31020794:2386","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/ab.bib.12.20150123.full.mrc:879243310:3725","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_012.bib.mrc:291048228:5714"],"title":"Missions d'évangélisation et circulation des savoirs","notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Knowledge Unlatched 103166 OpenEdition Books Select 2018: HSS Backlist B\n\nFrench."},"links":[{"url":"http://www.oapen.org/download?type=document&docid=1005194","title":"Access full text online"},{"url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/legalcode","title":"Creative Commons License"}],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/fre"},{"key":"/languages/spa"},{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"subjects":["History of religion"],"publish_country":"xx","key":"/books/OL28354145M","isbn_13":["9788496820524","9788490962466"],"works":[{"key":"/works/OL20927541W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"lc_classifications":["BV2185.C37 M57 2011"],"oclc_numbers":["730398286"],"number_of_pages":522,"publish_date":"2011","latest_revision":4,"revision":4,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2020-07-21T03:25:58.213163"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2025-08-08T01:34:49.274978"}}},"ISBN:9788496820524":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9788496820524","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL28354145M/Missions_d'évangélisation_et_circulation_des_savoirs","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL28354145M/Missions_d'évangélisation_et_circulation_des_savoirs","details":{"publishers":["Casa de Velázquez"],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Quels furent les savoirs utilisés, diffusés et produits par les missionnaires catholiques, à partir du milieu du XVIe siècle, aussi bien en Europe, qu'en Amérique, en Asie et en Afrique ? Dans quelle mesure l'entreprise d'évangélisation des âmes, jugées par les missionnaires comme païennes, hérétiques ou simplement indifférentes, a-t-elle participé à l'aventure moderne de la circulation des savoirs ? Ces questions intéressent aussi bien l'histoire sociale et culturelle des missions que l'histoire des empires et des sociétés coloniales ou l'histoire intellectuelle. Elles conduisent à réfléchir sur la manière dont l'Europe, à l'époque moderne, est entrée en relation avec d'autres espaces. À la croisée des croyances et des connaissances, les missions d'évangélisation ont suscité de profonds changements dans l'architecture des savoirs et ont paradoxalement participé à la sécularisation de la conception du monde."},"source_records":["marc:marc_oapen/oapen.marc.utf8.mrc:2334283:1982","marc:marc_oapen/convert_oapen_20201117.mrc:31020794:2386","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/ab.bib.12.20150123.full.mrc:879243310:3725","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_012.bib.mrc:291048228:5714"],"title":"Missions d'évangélisation et circulation des savoirs","notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Knowledge Unlatched 103166 OpenEdition Books Select 2018: HSS Backlist B\n\nFrench."},"links":[{"url":"http://www.oapen.org/download?type=document&docid=1005194","title":"Access full text online"},{"url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/legalcode","title":"Creative Commons License"}],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/fre"},{"key":"/languages/spa"},{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"subjects":["History of religion"],"publish_country":"xx","key":"/books/OL28354145M","isbn_13":["9788496820524","9788490962466"],"works":[{"key":"/works/OL20927541W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"lc_classifications":["BV2185.C37 M57 2011"],"oclc_numbers":["730398286"],"number_of_pages":522,"publish_date":"2011","latest_revision":4,"revision":4,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2020-07-21T03:25:58.213163"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2025-08-08T01:34:49.274978"}}},"ISBN:9781928396581":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9781928396581","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL28354581M/Nicholas_Bhekinkosi_Hepworth_Bhengu_s_Lasting_Legacy","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL28354581M/Nicholas_Bhekinkosi_Hepworth_Bhengu_s_Lasting_Legacy","details":{"publishers":["AOSIS"],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"This is a scholarly book that commemorates the legacy of Rev. Nicholas Bhekinkosi Hepworth Bhengu who was born on 05 September 1909 at eNtumeni, KwaZulu-Natal, South Africa. He was the founder of the Back to God Crusade in the 1950s that has become institutionalised within the Assemblies of God. He taught his church to be self-sustaining and also encouraged material independence through hard work. He died on 07 October 1985 at Groote Schuur Hospital in Cape Town, Western Cape, South Africa, leaving many people in Africa influenced by his rich legacy as an evangelist, pastor, teacher and church planter to this day. \r\n\r\nBhengu combined evangelism with development, which was critical for the black people who were under a repressive regime in South Africa and in sub-Saharan Africa. He was a religious revolutionary who ?planted? more than 2000 churches in South Africa and neighbouring countries by emphasising non-denominationalism without pressurising converts to discard their churches and join others. He was determined to build a movement that would be a vehicle to reach out to the continent of Africa through his churches. The book aims at providing academics and researchers with reference material of interactions between spirituality, church dynamics, socio-economic development and political environment. Its contribution to existing research with regard to the formative growth of Christianity in Africa is significant and innovative. The book?s target audience includes academics in the religious fields of missiology, church history and contextual theology, specifically researchers with intent to write scientific commentaries on the life history of Bhengu.\r\n"},"links":[{"url":"http://www.oapen.org/download?type=document&docid=1004791","title":"Access full text online"},{"url":"http://creative-commons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/","title":"License"}],"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2020-07-21T03:32:23.110759"},"latest_revision":1,"key":"/books/OL28354581M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL8010855A","name":"Dan S.B. Lephoko"}],"publish_places":["Durbanville"],"isbn_13":["9781928396581"],"pagination":"350","source_records":["marc:marc_oapen/oapen.marc.utf8.mrc:3072550:2675"],"title":"Nicholas Bhekinkosi Hepworth Bhengu?s Lasting Legacy","notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"English."},"number_of_pages":350,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2020-07-21T03:32:23.110759"},"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"subjects":["Christian mission & evangelism","History of religion"],"publish_country":"xx","works":[{"key":"/works/OL20927947W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"revision":1}},"ISBN:9789517463577":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9789517463577","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL3758711M/Strategies_of_sanity_and_survival","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL3758711M/Strategies_of_sanity_and_survival","details":{"publishers":["Finnish Literature Society"],"identifiers":{"librarything":["915575"],"goodreads":["983374"]},"subtitle":"religious responses to natural disasters in the Middle Ages","isbn_10":["951746357X"],"series":["Studia Fennica.","2"],"lc_classifications":["MLCM 2005/00921 (B)","BT161 .H36 2002","GB5014 .H36 2002"],"key":"/books/OL3758711M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL251801A","name":"Jussi Hanska"}],"publish_places":["Helsinki [Finland]"],"pagination":"220 p. :","source_records":["marc:marc_oapen/oapen.marc.utf8.mrc:11696577:1813","marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part31.utf8:74727925:865","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-009.mrc:152668087:1377","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/ab.bib.09.20150123.full.mrc:133605432:816"],"title":"Strategies of sanity and survival","lccn":["2003458811"],"notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Text in English with some Latin.\nIncludes bibliographical references (p. 202-210) and indexes."},"number_of_pages":220,"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"subjects":["Katastrofer -- religiösa aspekter","Digerdöden -- religiösa aspekter"],"publish_date":"2002","publish_country":"fi ","by_statement":"Jussi Hanska.","works":[{"key":"/works/OL2061783W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"oclc_numbers":["51902698"],"latest_revision":9,"revision":9,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-01T03:28:50.625462"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2024-09-02T09:19:01.834925"}}},"ISBN:9783161581632":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9783161581632","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL28324546M/Banned_Birds","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL28324546M/Banned_Birds","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/13290944-S.jpg","details":{"publishers":["Mohr Siebeck"],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"The dietary prohibitions in Leviticus 11 and Deuteronomy 14 represent one of the most detailed textual overlaps in the Pentateuch between the Priestly material and Deuteronomy. This is especially the case for the birds: their identities are shrouded in mystery and the reasons for their prohibition debated. Peter Altmann attempts to break this impasse by setting these flyers within the broader context of birds and flying creatures in the Ancient Near East. His investigation considers the zooarcheological data on birds in the ancient Levant, iconographic and textual material on mundane and mythic flyers from Egypt and Mesopotamia, as well as studying the symbolic functions of birds within the texts of the Hebrew Bible itself."},"source_records":["marc:marc_oapen/oapen.marc.mrc:10452:1813","marc:marc_oapen/oapen.marc.utf8.mrc:10482:1813","bwb:9783161581632","marc:marc_oapen/convert_oapen_20201117.mrc:9787408:2118","amazon:3161581636","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_019.bib.mrc:145832800:1340"],"title":"Banned Birds","notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Knowledge Unlatched 104938 KU Open Services\n\nEnglish."},"links":[{"url":"http://www.oapen.org/download?type=document&docid=1006691","title":"External source"},{"url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/legalcode","title":"license"}],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"subjects":["History of religion"],"publish_country":"xx","key":"/books/OL28324546M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL3192866A","name":"Peter Altmann"}],"isbn_13":["9783161581632","9783161581649"],"works":[{"key":"/works/OL20909530W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"covers":[13290944],"number_of_pages":186,"publish_date":"Dec 01, 2019","oclc_numbers":["1134853229"],"identifiers":{"dnb":["1196568286"]},"latest_rev